WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:09.744
How does inbound stock move from receipt to storage? These
Quark WMS recordings show receiving and putaway as
separate operations.

2
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:18.360
Start in the web application. The receipt list provides
the inbound context. Open the receipt to review the
document.

3
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:30.131
Review the receipt and its lines before following the
receiving operation on RF.

4
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:43.564
On the RF terminal, the operator opens receiving and
identifies the advance shipping notice, or ASN.

5
00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:01.433
Identify the SKU to receive before entering the received
quantity.

6
00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:10.304
Enter the quantity received. This example shows a staging
destination.

7
00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:22.330
The workflow returns to SKU entry, then ends at the
receipt summary.

8
00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:28.147
A separate putaway example.

9
00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:32.508
Open Putaway from the RF inventory menu.

10
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:40.155
Identify the pallet by its license plate number, or LPN.

11
00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:49.103
Review the pallet details and confirm the stock.

12
00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:58.605
The RF screen shows the destination. Move the pallet and
confirm the location.

13
00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:07.896
The Put Away screen confirms storage placement at the
selected location.

14
00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:19.204
Explore inbound workflows on quark.build. Use Discuss Your
Warehouse Project to talk through your own warehouse
process.
